; setline_model_accepts_out_of_domain_value: models are unbounded.
;
; A model's linear entry is a bias coefficient, not an assignment. Its
; magnitude is the weight the objective gives that variable and has nothing
; to do with the values the variable may take, so a binary model routinely
; carries negative and large biases. Only samples carry a domain the VM
; enforces.
;
; This is the scope vector: it fails the moment the check is applied by
; register kind rather than by mode, which is the single easiest way to get
; this change wrong.

PUSH 2
BQMX r0          ; binary MODEL, not a sample

PUSH 0
PUSH -7          ; a bias, and not an assignment
SETLINE r0

PUSH 0
GETLINE r0
STOW r1
PUSH 0
OUTPUT r1        ; outputs[0] = -7
HALT
